---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteBase } from "../utils/site.js";
import latestRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-60bec66.json";
import focusedRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/miniwob-targeted-browser-fixes-8490bd7.json";

const episodeCount = latestRun.episodeCount;
const successCount = latestRun.successCount;
const failureCount = episodeCount - successCount;
const successPercent = Math.round(latestRun.taskSuccessRate * 100);
const environment = latestRun.rawRecords[0];
const commitUrl = `https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/commit/${latestRun.suite.agentDecisionKitCommit}`;
const rawRunUrl = "https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-60bec66.json";
---

<BaseLayout title="Real Browser Automation Benchmarks | Agent Decision Kit" description="Reproducible Playwright and BrowserGym MiniWoB results for Agent Decision Kit, with task success, latency, environment details, and raw episodes." canonicalPath="benchmarks/">
  <main class="page">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">MEASURED RUNS · RAW EPISODES INCLUDED</p>
      <h1>Browser automation<br /><span>with the limits in view.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Real BrowserGym MiniWoB runs from this repository. Each report keeps task success, latency, failures, and the environment together so a small smoke run stays a small claim.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="latest" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">LATEST MULTI-TOOL INTEGRATION</p>
        <h2 id="latest-title">{successCount} of {episodeCount} tasks succeeded.</h2>
        <p>The bounded harness copied explicit values from synthetic task instructions, selected visible native options, and exercised <code>browser_set_range</code> on keyboard-operated sliders. It measures tool integration, not an autonomous coding-agent score. The slider task passed after its Submit action received the runner's local-only synthetic approval; the no-progress guard stopped a repeated no-op, and visual inspection described two pages without acting.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="success-chart">
        <div class="bar" role="img" aria-label={`${successCount} tasks succeeded and ${failureCount} tasks did not succeed, out of ${episodeCount}`}>
          <span class="passed" style={`width:${successPercent}%`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="failed" style={`width:${100 - successPercent}%`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <span><i class="legend passed-key"></i>{successCount} succeeded</span>
          <span><i class="legend failed-key"></i>{failureCount} did not reach the task goal</span>
          <span>0 harness timeouts</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">TASK SUCCESS</p><strong>{successCount}/{episodeCount}</strong><span>{successPercent}% on this curated set</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">BROWSER LOOP P50</p><strong>{(latestRun.agentActionLatencyMs.p50 / 1000).toFixed(2)}s</strong><span>Includes tool actions and inspection</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">BROWSER LOOP P95</p><strong>{(latestRun.agentActionLatencyMs.p95 / 1000).toFixed(1)}s</strong><span>Two local vision descriptions drive the slow tail</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">DECISION CALL P95</p><strong>{latestRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.p95}ms</strong><span>Cold call in a new Node process per task</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="conditions" aria-labelledby="conditions-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">REPRODUCTION DETAILS</p>
        <h2 id="conditions-title">A CPU run with a fixed task set.</h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Agent Decision Kit</dt><dd><a href={commitUrl}>{latestRun.suite.agentDecisionKitCommit.slice(0, 7)}</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Benchmark</dt><dd>BrowserGym MiniWoB 0.14.3</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Browser</dt><dd>{environment.browserVersion} · Node {environment.nodeVersion}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Machine</dt><dd>{environment.operatingSystem} · CPU</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Task set</dt><dd>26 curated MiniWoB tasks · seed 7 · eight actions per task</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Model path</dt><dd>Local semantic model and CPU visual fallback; no remote decision provider</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <b>How to read the latency</b>
        <p>Every task starts a fresh Node bridge. Six measured decision calls had p50 211 ms / p95 471 ms; this run does not establish warm throughput or the consumer-GPU target.</p>
        <p>Two visual-only pages used local image description on CPU and took tens of seconds. The tool reports this fallback as slower.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={rawRunUrl}>Inspect the summary and all raw episodes ↗</a>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="other-runs" aria-labelledby="other-runs-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">OTHER RECORDED RUNS</p>
      <h2 id="other-runs-title">Different runs answer different questions.</h2>
      <div class="run-list">
        <article>
          <div><strong>19/26</strong><span>Prior multi-tool baseline</span></div>
          <p>The same task set before support for MiniWoB's keyboard-operated sliders. It did not call <code>browser_set_range</code>; <code>use-slider-2</code> was the only task outcome that changed in the later run.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-b901f05.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>{focusedRun.successCount}/{focusedRun.episodeCount}</strong><span>Focused browser regressions</span></div>
          <p>Six previously troublesome MiniWoB cases on Linux CPU. Browser action-loop p50 258 ms / p95 721 ms, with zero semantic model calls. This is a targeted regression set, not a general success estimate.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-targeted-browser-fixes-8490bd7.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>8/8</strong><span>Focused MiniWoB smoke</span></div>
          <p>Eight curated tasks on Linux CPU. Browser action-loop p50 305 ms / p95 699 ms. One integration run; not a general success estimate.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-pointer-fastpath-diagnostic-rerun-smoke.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>3/26</strong><span>Decision/action only</span></div>
          <p>A broader task mix that repeatedly called the decision/action tool without orchestrating form fills, native select options, or visual inspection.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-smoke-suite.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">The task sets and harnesses differ, so these counts are not a controlled comparison. No Jev parity comparison has been run. WebArena and VisualWebArena need their separately configured benchmark services; neither has a result in this repository.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/README.md">Read the full protocol and reproduction commands →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="prerequisites" aria-labelledby="prerequisites-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">BROADER BROWSERGYM SETUPS</p>
      <h2 id="prerequisites-title">WebArena scores need running benchmark sites.</h2>
      <p class="prerequisite-lead">Installing BrowserGym alone does not provide the WebArena or VisualWebArena sites. Their BrowserGym integrations need a set of configured domain URLs; none are configured in the recorded environment, so this page does not report results for those suites.</p>
      <div class="setup-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>WebArena</h3>
          <p>Requires URLs for the shopping site and admin, Reddit, GitLab, Wikipedia, map, and homepage.</p>
          <code>WA_SHOPPING · WA_REDDIT · WA_GITLAB · WA_WIKIPEDIA · WA_MAP · WA_HOMEPAGE</code>
          <a href="https://github.com/ServiceNow/BrowserGym/blob/main/browsergym/webarena/README.md">BrowserGym WebArena setup ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>VisualWebArena</h3>
          <p>Requires separate classifieds, shopping, Reddit, Wikipedia, and homepage URLs.</p>
          <code>VWA_CLASSIFIEDS · VWA_SHOPPING · VWA_REDDIT · VWA_WIKIPEDIA · VWA_HOMEPAGE</code>
          <a href="https://github.com/ServiceNow/BrowserGym/blob/main/browsergym/visualwebarena/README.md">BrowserGym VisualWebArena setup ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">The upstream WebArena guide notes that some fuzzy-match evaluations call a hosted GPT-4 judge. The default Agent Decision Kit benchmark path stays local and does not enable paid judging. See the <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/README.md#webarena-and-visualwebarena-prerequisites">prerequisites and evaluator policy</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:72px 28px}.eyebrow{color:var(--mint);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase}.intro{max-width:820px;margin-bottom:68px}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(46px,7vw,78px);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:18px 0}.intro h1 span{color:var(--mint)}.lead{max-width:720px;color:var(--muted);font-size:18px;line-height:1.65}.latest{padding:34px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#102538,#0b1725)}.section-heading{max-width:790px}.section-heading h2,.conditions h2,.other-runs h2,.prerequisites h2{font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,42px);letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:12px 0}.section-heading>p:last-child{max-width:760px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}.success-chart{margin:34px 0 38px}.bar{height:24px;display:flex;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#17283a}.bar span{display:block;height:100%}.passed{background:var(--mint)}.failed{background:#64748b}.success-chart figcaption{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:22px;margin-top:13px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.success-chart figcaption span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.legend{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px;display:inline-block}.passed-key{background:var(--mint)}.failed-key{background:#64748b}.metrics-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px}.metric{min-height:135px;padding:19px;border:1px solid #2b4156;border-radius:13px;background:#091522}.metric strong{display:block;font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:5px 0 2px}.metric span{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;line-height:1.45}.metric .eyebrow{margin:0}.conditions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .78fr;gap:52px;padding:74px 12px}.conditions dl{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:26px}.conditions dl div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:170px 1fr;gap:14px;padding:13px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}dt{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}dd{margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5}aside{align-self:center;padding:25px;background:#0d1b2b;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:15px}aside b{font-size:15px}aside p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65}.text-link{display:inline-flex;margin-top:9px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.other-runs{padding:54px 0 16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.run-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin:28px 0}.run-list article{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:var(--panel)}.run-list article>div{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px}.run-list strong{font-size:33px;letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--mint)}.run-list span{font-weight:700;font-size:13px}.run-list p,.comparison-note,.prerequisite-lead,.setup-grid p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.65}.run-list a{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.comparison-note{max-width:850px;margin:24px 0}.prerequisites{padding:54px 0 20px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.prerequisite-lead{max-width:780px}.setup-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin:25px 0}.setup-grid article{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:var(--panel)}.setup-grid h3{font-size:20px;margin:0}.setup-grid p{margin:12px 0}.setup-grid code{display:block;padding:11px 12px;border-radius:8px;background:#08111f;color:var(--mint);font-size:11px;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.setup-grid a{display:inline-flex;margin-top:14px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}
  @media(max-width:850px){.metrics-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.conditions{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:25px}.intro{margin-bottom:48px}}
  @media(max-width:560px){.page{padding:52px 20px}.latest{padding:22px}.metrics-grid,.run-list,.setup-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.conditions{padding:54px 0}.conditions dl div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:5px}.success-chart figcaption{gap:10px;flex-direction:column}}
</style>
